say rbx holds an address
1) mov rax, [rbx]
 -> This will copy 8 bytes from that address  and put it to rax
 use mov al, [rbx] -> to tell cpu to go to that address and decode info and copy only 1 byte.
 ---- The output register here is defining how many bytes to copy




mul instruction:
        mul rbx
        -> multiplies rbx and rax
        -> result stored as rdx:rax
                           rdx     rax
                        [64bits][64bits]

div instruction:
        div rbx
        -> it does [rdx]: [rax] / rbx
        -> quotient in rax, remainder in rdx
        Remeber to CLEAR rdx before div


